1
00:00:50,544 --> 00:00:53,964
MY BIAS, MY BOSS

2
00:01:02,597 --> 00:01:05,350
There's quite a competition
to launch their brand with us.

3
00:01:05,642 --> 00:01:07,310
There are over 30 brands

4
00:01:07,394 --> 00:01:09,020
that have sent us samples
just this week.

5
00:01:09,604 --> 00:01:12,649
Many of these are dupes of what I saw
at the last Paris Fashion Week.

6
00:01:13,024 --> 00:01:15,277
It had many innovative designs

7
00:01:15,360 --> 00:01:17,654
so it looks like domestic brands
were heavily influenced.

8
00:01:17,737 --> 00:01:19,990
If all they can do is copy

9
00:01:20,073 --> 00:01:21,783
they can't work with Appello.

10
00:01:22,909 --> 00:01:24,244
I'll look into just this brand.

11
00:01:24,995 --> 00:01:27,581
All right.
Ms. Seo, please help out with that.

12
00:01:27,664 --> 00:01:29,749
I'll join you right away
after figuring out the display.

13
00:01:29,833 --> 00:01:32,919
Yes, I'll get the models ready
for the fitting.

14
00:01:33,003 --> 00:01:34,546
- Okay, tell me when they're ready.
- Yes, sir.

15
00:01:37,882 --> 00:01:38,925
This is just like you.

16
00:01:39,718 --> 00:01:41,469
They aren't generic

17
00:01:42,721 --> 00:01:44,389
and they carry their own identity.

18
00:01:44,472 --> 00:01:46,224
That's how Appello started.

19
00:01:46,308 --> 00:01:48,268
I was just collecting the clothes
I wanted to wear

20
00:01:48,351 --> 00:01:49,811
which turned
into a tiny curated boutique.

21
00:01:50,604 --> 00:01:53,398
And now, it's a platform
that carries hundreds of brands.

22
00:01:54,024 --> 00:01:55,567
The pressure is different now.

23
00:01:56,109 --> 00:01:58,111
Which you're carrying very well.

24
00:01:58,194 --> 00:01:59,237
I'm in charge of the direction.

25
00:01:59,654 --> 00:02:02,449
And if that direction is too skewed,
everyone who's following will fall.

26
00:02:02,741 --> 00:02:04,367
Gosh, I know

27
00:02:04,451 --> 00:02:05,952
that this is the time
to be more inclusive.

28
00:02:10,040 --> 00:02:11,124
Yes, sir.

29
00:02:12,417 --> 00:02:15,712
Yes, Mr. Kang. I'll do as you say
and pick up more mainstream designs.

30
00:02:20,300 --> 00:02:22,385
EPISODE 2

31
00:02:24,763 --> 00:02:26,014
Okay.

32
00:02:26,097 --> 00:02:28,224
That bracelet on the man's hand.

33
00:02:28,308 --> 00:02:29,517
- Take note of it.
- Yes.

34
00:02:32,270 --> 00:02:35,065
Please get a tie
that's as bright as this one.

35
00:02:35,148 --> 00:02:36,650
Right. Yes, sir.

36
00:02:37,692 --> 00:02:38,777
Great work, everyone.

37
00:02:39,402 --> 00:02:40,445
- Yes.
- Goodbye.

38
00:02:40,528 --> 00:02:42,155
Text me the pictures we took today.

39
00:02:42,238 --> 00:02:45,492
- Okay. Goodbye, Mr. Lee.
- Okay.

40
00:03:07,389 --> 00:03:10,684
D.N.X! D.N.X! We love you, D.N.X!

41
00:03:30,662 --> 00:03:32,914
You dropped this.

42
00:03:41,631 --> 00:03:43,550
Right. Thank you.

43
00:03:48,388 --> 00:03:49,389
Getting in?

44
00:03:50,640 --> 00:03:51,641
What?

45
00:03:53,351 --> 00:03:55,520
Oh, I am.

46
00:04:11,661 --> 00:04:12,954
Don't be so nervous, Da-reum.

47
00:04:13,037 --> 00:04:15,165
Try to act as naturally as possible.

48
00:04:22,088 --> 00:04:23,214
NAM DA-REUM

49
00:04:24,424 --> 00:04:26,176
- You must be one of the new hires.
- Sorry?

50
00:04:31,222 --> 00:04:32,223
Yes.

51
00:04:32,807 --> 00:04:34,100
Why weren't you there
at the welcome dinner?

52
00:04:37,562 --> 00:04:39,773
I got a bit drunk last night

53
00:04:40,607 --> 00:04:41,900
and went home early.

54
00:04:42,942 --> 00:04:44,736
I see.

55
00:04:46,863 --> 00:04:48,823
Anyway, it's nice to meet you,
Da-reum.

56
00:04:53,411 --> 00:04:54,871
How do you know my name?

57
00:04:56,623 --> 00:04:57,791
I look forward to working with you.

58
00:05:12,138 --> 00:05:13,556
I'll do my best.

59
00:05:17,143 --> 00:05:18,144
See you around.

60
00:05:20,188 --> 00:05:21,523
Yes, Mr. Lee.

61
00:05:28,696 --> 00:05:29,906
Goodbye.

62
00:05:51,052 --> 00:05:52,220
My gosh.

63
00:05:53,555 --> 00:05:55,223
My gosh!

64
00:05:55,306 --> 00:05:58,977
I shook hands with Chan!

65
00:06:01,145 --> 00:06:02,814
My gosh!

66
00:06:05,692 --> 00:06:07,944
Great job on not getting too nervous.

67
00:06:08,027 --> 00:06:09,571
Good one, Da-reum.

68
00:06:23,793 --> 00:06:24,961
Goodbye.

69
00:06:32,969 --> 00:06:37,265
WOLHWA SILVER WORKSHOP

70
00:06:49,819 --> 00:06:53,406
Hey, what have you been
doing here for days?

71
00:06:54,365 --> 00:06:56,075
Are you looking for a career change?

72
00:06:56,367 --> 00:06:57,535
Should I do that?

73
00:06:59,078 --> 00:07:00,663
D.N.X has disbanded

74
00:07:00,747 --> 00:07:02,749
and not many would remember Lee Chan.

75
00:07:04,417 --> 00:07:05,418
Hey.

76
00:07:05,960 --> 00:07:07,045
I'm pretty good, aren't I?

77
00:07:07,879 --> 00:07:10,381
You might as well
open a jewelry studio.

78
00:07:13,593 --> 00:07:16,804
Hey, clean up everything
before I come back.

79
00:07:16,888 --> 00:07:17,889
Okay?

80
00:07:18,389 --> 00:07:19,515
Okay?

81
00:07:46,334 --> 00:07:48,378
- Hello.
- Hello.

82
00:07:48,461 --> 00:07:50,505
By any chance, how much is this?

83
00:07:50,964 --> 00:07:54,467
This is a DIY jewelry studio,
so we do not sell any items.

84
00:07:54,550 --> 00:07:57,011
This was
one of our customers' designs.

85
00:07:57,345 --> 00:08:01,516
This is the exact shape
that my all-time favorite celebrity

86
00:08:01,599 --> 00:08:03,601
always draws
when he signs autographs.

87
00:08:04,477 --> 00:08:05,979
Today's my birthday

88
00:08:06,062 --> 00:08:08,272
so I want to buy it for myself
as a gift.

89
00:08:08,356 --> 00:08:09,816
Can I please buy it?

90
00:08:10,858 --> 00:08:12,276
I'm sorry.

91
00:08:12,360 --> 00:08:14,654
But why don't you
try making it yourself?

92
00:08:16,447 --> 00:08:19,450
I don't think
I can make it look exactly the same.

93
00:08:19,534 --> 00:08:23,287
It's not as difficult as you think.

94
00:08:25,581 --> 00:08:26,833
It's okay.

95
00:08:27,583 --> 00:08:29,877
I understand. Thank you.

96
00:08:29,961 --> 00:08:31,587
- Sure.
- Goodbye.

97
00:08:31,671 --> 00:08:32,880
Okay. Goodbye.

98
00:08:36,134 --> 00:08:39,262
WOLHWA SILVER WORKSHOP

99
00:08:56,070 --> 00:08:57,405
It was you from back then.

100
00:09:02,118 --> 00:09:04,954
- Great work today.
- Goodbye!

101
00:09:05,913 --> 00:09:09,250
We've all done so well today!
See you tomorrow.

102
00:09:09,625 --> 00:09:12,336
See you tomorrow! Bye!

103
00:09:13,796 --> 00:09:17,884
It looks like something great
must've happened to Da-reum.

104
00:09:17,967 --> 00:09:20,762
Right? Our team has been
swamped with work lately.

105
00:09:21,095 --> 00:09:24,182
Min-a, if it's okay with you

106
00:09:24,265 --> 00:09:25,975
why don't we grab a glass of beer?

107
00:09:26,059 --> 00:09:28,102
Gosh, beer?

108
00:09:29,020 --> 00:09:30,104
No.

109
00:09:32,148 --> 00:09:33,191
No?

110
00:09:39,781 --> 00:09:41,282
You must be one of the new hires.

111
00:09:48,372 --> 00:09:49,540
SUNGJU STATION

112
00:09:53,419 --> 00:09:54,587
It's nice to meet you, Da-reum.

113
00:09:56,506 --> 00:09:59,467
It was so great to meet you.

114
00:10:05,056 --> 00:10:06,307
See you around.

115
00:10:19,362 --> 00:10:21,114
See you!

116
00:10:21,197 --> 00:10:23,533
Chan, let us meet again!

117
00:10:23,616 --> 00:10:25,034
See you, Da-reum!

118
00:10:26,410 --> 00:10:27,537
Bye!

119
00:10:32,250 --> 00:10:33,501
Are you that happy?

120
00:10:35,044 --> 00:10:36,045
Yes.

121
00:10:36,587 --> 00:10:38,756
Someone might think
you just won the lottery.

122
00:10:38,840 --> 00:10:40,466
It's her ultimate fan moment.

123
00:10:40,550 --> 00:10:43,177
Fans who lived outside Seoul
can't go to music show recordings.

124
00:10:43,261 --> 00:10:47,849
And at concerts, they look this small
so you can't even see their faces.

125
00:10:48,391 --> 00:10:50,810
You've made it, Namda.

126
00:10:50,893 --> 00:10:53,688
So? Would you like to smell my hand?

127
00:10:53,771 --> 00:10:55,273
Jeez.

128
00:10:55,356 --> 00:10:57,024
- No!
- Me too!

129
00:10:57,108 --> 00:11:00,111
No, it's going to wear off.
I can't lose it!

130
00:11:02,530 --> 00:11:04,866
Today is the first time
I've seen Chan in person.

131
00:11:05,992 --> 00:11:08,578
I'll always celebrate this day.

132
00:11:08,661 --> 00:11:11,414
You've always insisted
Chan gave you that necklace.

133
00:11:11,747 --> 00:11:13,666
Do you finally admit
that you were overly hopeful?

134
00:11:19,380 --> 00:11:23,968
But no one else
could have possibly made this.

135
00:11:36,022 --> 00:11:37,148
Excuse me.

136
00:11:42,320 --> 00:11:43,321
Happy birthday.

137
00:12:17,980 --> 00:12:20,900
He definitely sounded like him too.

138
00:12:20,983 --> 00:12:24,028
You're just misremembering
as a hopeful fan.

139
00:12:25,655 --> 00:12:26,822
You think so?

140
00:12:27,073 --> 00:12:28,241
Well, anyway.

141
00:12:28,324 --> 00:12:32,078
I finally met him in person. My gosh!

142
00:12:32,161 --> 00:12:33,829
I'm not dreaming, am I?

143
00:12:35,748 --> 00:12:37,124
It hurts!

144
00:12:37,208 --> 00:12:38,251
- It's not.
- It hurts.

145
00:12:38,334 --> 00:12:40,044
APPELLO

146
00:12:42,213 --> 00:12:44,215
This time, the overseas training
for outstanding employees

147
00:12:44,298 --> 00:12:46,217
will be held
at the New York Fashion Week.

148
00:12:46,592 --> 00:12:47,593
New York?

149
00:12:47,969 --> 00:12:49,220
It sounds perfect.

150
00:12:49,637 --> 00:12:51,180
You'll get to see a lot

151
00:12:52,431 --> 00:12:54,642
and also have a mountain of work.

152
00:12:55,184 --> 00:12:57,603
Overseas training
for outstanding employees?

153
00:12:58,104 --> 00:13:00,439
It's a tradition of sorts
that Director Lee has made

154
00:13:00,523 --> 00:13:02,942
since the foundation of Appello.

155
00:13:03,025 --> 00:13:04,735
Once a year,
we pick out an outstanding employee

156
00:13:04,819 --> 00:13:06,195
to do a project abroad.

157
00:13:06,862 --> 00:13:09,657
Someone will be chosen
early next year.

158
00:13:11,075 --> 00:13:13,119
Thank you. Come here, Min-a.

159
00:13:14,120 --> 00:13:15,454
Does that mean

160
00:13:15,830 --> 00:13:17,748
Director Lee will go on the trip too?

161
00:13:17,832 --> 00:13:18,916
Of course.

162
00:13:19,375 --> 00:13:21,669
He has never missed it once.

163
00:13:21,752 --> 00:13:23,629
Who picks out
the outstanding employee?

164
00:13:23,713 --> 00:13:24,714
Mr. Kang.

165
00:13:27,800 --> 00:13:29,093
Mr. Kang?

166
00:13:40,813 --> 00:13:42,064
AVOID MR. KANG

167
00:13:42,481 --> 00:13:43,482
WORK HARD!

168
00:13:47,653 --> 00:13:49,488
EMPLOYEE OVERSEAS TRAINING!
GET ON MR. KANG'S GOOD SIDE!

169
00:13:53,117 --> 00:13:54,243
Well...

170
00:13:55,036 --> 00:13:58,789
Is it okay
for my goal to change so drastically?

171
00:13:59,957 --> 00:14:02,168
No, Da-reum.

172
00:14:02,710 --> 00:14:04,462
You can do this.

173
00:14:07,131 --> 00:14:08,215
First of all

174
00:14:09,550 --> 00:14:13,220
I must figure out
what Mr. Kang is like.

175
00:14:16,932 --> 00:14:19,185
Ms. Kim, this is for you.

176
00:14:22,104 --> 00:14:23,814
Ms. Kim.

177
00:14:24,148 --> 00:14:26,776
So what does Mr. Kang like?

178
00:14:27,526 --> 00:14:28,569
Why are you asking about him?

179
00:14:30,571 --> 00:14:34,575
I wasn't exactly
on my best behavior since day one

180
00:14:35,117 --> 00:14:36,744
so I wanted to improve my reputation

181
00:14:36,827 --> 00:14:38,621
and do my best at work.

182
00:14:39,663 --> 00:14:40,706
Is that so?

183
00:14:41,248 --> 00:14:42,792
Mr. Kang...

184
00:14:44,835 --> 00:14:48,214
He only uses the brown capsules
for the coffee machine.

185
00:14:51,759 --> 00:14:52,885
The brown ones?

186
00:14:53,844 --> 00:14:55,054
Chocolate latte.

187
00:14:55,137 --> 00:14:56,972
He has a sweet tooth,
unlike how he seems.

188
00:14:58,015 --> 00:14:59,767
GUIDE TO WINNING CEO KANG HA-GI
OFFER HIM CHOCOLATE LATTE

189
00:15:06,899 --> 00:15:08,526
Mr. Kang.

190
00:15:08,609 --> 00:15:10,903
Would you like
a cup of sweet chocolate latte?

191
00:15:10,986 --> 00:15:12,154
I made it just now.

192
00:15:15,533 --> 00:15:18,327
No, I only drink one cup a day
because of my blood glucose level.

193
00:15:18,411 --> 00:15:20,496
I've already had it,
so enjoy it for yourself.

194
00:15:25,668 --> 00:15:26,669
Okay.

195
00:15:26,752 --> 00:15:28,587
GUIDE TO WINNING CEO KANG HA-GI
CROSS OUT CHOCOLATE LATTE

196
00:15:30,131 --> 00:15:33,801
I think he spends time on the rooftop
right after eating lunch.

197
00:15:33,884 --> 00:15:36,679
He likes to spend at least 20 minutes
a day in the sun.

198
00:15:36,762 --> 00:15:38,097
GUIDE TO WINNING CEO KANG HA-GI
BE SUNLIGHT BUDDIES

199
00:15:45,771 --> 00:15:49,692
Oh, my.
I didn't know you came here too.

200
00:15:49,817 --> 00:15:51,402
Great view, isn't it?

201
00:15:51,485 --> 00:15:52,528
Yes.

202
00:15:53,904 --> 00:15:56,949
I always get my share of sunlight

203
00:15:57,032 --> 00:15:58,868
whenever I'm done with lunch.

204
00:15:58,951 --> 00:16:01,495
People need sunlight to stay healthy.

205
00:16:01,871 --> 00:16:05,458
Mr. Kang, people these days
are often low on vitamin D.

206
00:16:05,541 --> 00:16:07,168
- Ms. Nam.
- Yes?

207
00:16:12,965 --> 00:16:15,134
You're very distracting.
And don't stand in my view.

208
00:16:18,179 --> 00:16:19,180
Right.

209
00:16:19,597 --> 00:16:20,764
I'm sorry.

210
00:16:23,142 --> 00:16:24,935
GUIDE TO WINNING CEO KANG HA-GI
CROSS OUT SUNLIGHT BUDDIES

211
00:16:26,145 --> 00:16:29,064
Also, when you compliment him
on his style

212
00:16:29,148 --> 00:16:30,524
he gets somewhat pleased.

213
00:16:30,608 --> 00:16:32,109
GUIDE TO WINNING CEO KANG HA-GI
COMPLIMENT HIM

214
00:16:33,235 --> 00:16:35,738
My gosh, Mr. Kang.

215
00:16:35,821 --> 00:16:39,492
You look so cool
in that shirt and tie.

216
00:16:39,575 --> 00:16:40,993
You could be a runway model.

217
00:16:41,076 --> 00:16:43,078
I pulled an all-nighter,
so it's the same as yesterday.

218
00:16:47,875 --> 00:16:49,126
Goodbye.

219
00:16:52,421 --> 00:16:53,756
GUIDE TO WINNING CEO KANG HA-GI
CROSS OUT COMPLIMENTS

220
00:16:53,839 --> 00:16:56,050
How come nothing is working?

221
00:17:05,768 --> 00:17:09,063
You look so cool
in that shirt and tie.

222
00:17:09,480 --> 00:17:10,898
You could be a runway model.

223
00:17:18,364 --> 00:17:19,448
My gosh.

224
00:17:25,829 --> 00:17:27,915
I looked into Ms. Nam

225
00:17:27,998 --> 00:17:29,667
and she recently quit...

226
00:17:29,750 --> 00:17:32,002
Just speak normally.
It's just the two of us here.

227
00:17:32,461 --> 00:17:33,462
Yes, sir.

228
00:17:33,546 --> 00:17:36,966
Ms. Nam recently resigned
from her job at SE Corporation.

229
00:17:38,759 --> 00:17:42,263
I feel like she has a hidden agenda.

230
00:17:42,555 --> 00:17:44,640
Maybe she's a honey trap

231
00:17:44,723 --> 00:17:45,766
sent by Director Kim.

232
00:17:47,768 --> 00:17:48,811
Honey trap?

233
00:17:49,687 --> 00:17:50,688
I don't think so.

234
00:17:50,771 --> 00:17:52,314
Exactly. It's nonsense.

235
00:17:53,482 --> 00:17:56,026
How about a cuteness ploy?
Someone who traps you with cuteness.

236
00:17:59,655 --> 00:18:00,864
That also doesn't make sense.

237
00:18:01,240 --> 00:18:02,658
Is she here just to wreak havoc?

238
00:18:13,168 --> 00:18:16,171
How do I get on Mr. Kang's good side?

239
00:18:16,755 --> 00:18:18,465
- What's up?
- I mean

240
00:18:18,966 --> 00:18:22,469
whenever I say something,
all he says is, "No, thanks."

241
00:18:22,553 --> 00:18:25,389
There's no way to get through to him.

242
00:18:25,472 --> 00:18:27,224
It's not like I'm into him.

243
00:18:27,308 --> 00:18:28,809
I'm trying to be
the outstanding employee.

244
00:18:28,892 --> 00:18:31,186
Maybe he thinks
you're hitting on him.

245
00:18:31,270 --> 00:18:34,064
He just doesn't let anyone
get close to him.

246
00:18:34,148 --> 00:18:35,899
Is that why he shuts you off?

247
00:18:36,442 --> 00:18:38,527
No, he's like that
to everyone else too.

248
00:18:38,611 --> 00:18:40,279
That's why the employees

249
00:18:40,362 --> 00:18:42,615
nicknamed him Icy Kang.

250
00:18:42,698 --> 00:18:43,991
He's that cold.

251
00:18:44,074 --> 00:18:46,619
Hey, look at this.

252
00:18:46,702 --> 00:18:49,330
Exclusive! Former K-pop idol
and top actor A is allegedly gay.

253
00:18:49,413 --> 00:18:51,415
The boyfriend, B, is the current CEO
of his fashion platform.

254
00:18:51,498 --> 00:18:53,500
Rumors say he hired him
to keep their relationship secret.

255
00:18:53,584 --> 00:18:55,127
No way. That's obviously Appello.

256
00:18:55,210 --> 00:18:56,211
Totes. It's Appello.

257
00:18:56,295 --> 00:18:58,088
Wow, Lee Chan is gay?

258
00:18:58,172 --> 00:19:00,424
- He's gay?
- He's gay?

259
00:19:01,175 --> 00:19:04,928
Hey, are A and B here referring

260
00:19:05,220 --> 00:19:06,889
- to Chan and your CEO?
- What?

261
00:19:07,473 --> 00:19:08,474
What?

262
00:19:08,849 --> 00:19:09,850
Are they dating?

263
00:19:10,476 --> 00:19:11,977
What are you talking about?

264
00:19:12,519 --> 00:19:13,604
Chan is...

265
00:19:15,397 --> 00:19:16,649
a heterosexual.

266
00:19:16,732 --> 00:19:19,234
He once said in an interview
that an older girl at his high school

267
00:19:19,318 --> 00:19:20,611
was his first love.

268
00:19:21,153 --> 00:19:22,154
Then what is this?

269
00:19:22,237 --> 00:19:24,865
What do you think? A blind item
circulating in the financial world.

270
00:19:25,658 --> 00:19:28,118
Our company CEO and Chan?

271
00:19:28,619 --> 00:19:29,870
No way.

272
00:19:35,459 --> 00:19:36,794
No, impossible.

273
00:20:20,254 --> 00:20:21,797
Oh, come on.

274
00:20:30,139 --> 00:20:31,765
Hey, get up and eat.

275
00:20:46,196 --> 00:20:47,906
Yes, this is what I'm talking about.

276
00:20:48,449 --> 00:20:50,033
Wait, aren't you eating?

277
00:20:50,701 --> 00:20:52,077
This is how I eat breakfast.

278
00:20:53,454 --> 00:20:56,707
Hey, grabbing a drink was an excuse.
You came to eat that, right?

279
00:20:57,708 --> 00:20:58,709
Bingo.

280
00:21:03,088 --> 00:21:05,799
Gosh, yes. That hits the spot.

281
00:21:05,883 --> 00:21:07,885
It tastes just like your mother's...

282
00:21:18,854 --> 00:21:21,315
Gosh, it's so filling
to finally eat a home-cooked meal.

283
00:21:22,065 --> 00:21:23,442
Can I stay at your place for a while?

284
00:21:23,525 --> 00:21:26,403
No, I had to sleep on the couch,
and my back is killing me.

285
00:21:26,487 --> 00:21:27,613
We could've shared the bed.

286
00:21:29,406 --> 00:21:30,407
Are you insane?

287
00:21:31,408 --> 00:21:32,659
I'm running late.

288
00:21:32,743 --> 00:21:33,994
Eat, clean up, and go.

289
00:21:35,078 --> 00:21:36,079
Hey.

290
00:21:36,955 --> 00:21:38,999
Take this. You haven't even eaten.

291
00:21:39,583 --> 00:21:41,960
- What's this?
- I got it from someone I work with.

292
00:21:42,544 --> 00:21:44,004
It should be good.
If anything, they know good food.

293
00:21:44,755 --> 00:21:45,798
Take it.

294
00:21:48,300 --> 00:21:49,718
- Bye.
- Bye.

295
00:21:49,802 --> 00:21:50,886
Clean up before you go!

296
00:21:54,890 --> 00:21:56,225
CEO KANG HA-GI

297
00:23:02,499 --> 00:23:03,500
Come in.

298
00:23:03,917 --> 00:23:06,461
Mr. Kang, the weekly meeting
for the marketing team is ready.

299
00:23:06,545 --> 00:23:08,338
- Okay. I'll be there.
- Yes, sir.

300
00:23:28,191 --> 00:23:29,443
Jeez.

301
00:23:34,406 --> 00:23:36,992
Hey, come and take these now.

302
00:23:37,075 --> 00:23:39,620
Yes, for this lookbook shooting

303
00:23:39,703 --> 00:23:42,539
we want to focus on gorpcore

304
00:23:42,623 --> 00:23:45,626
as that is the trending aesthetic
at the moment.

305
00:23:52,633 --> 00:23:54,843
Hobbies that are on the rise

306
00:23:54,927 --> 00:23:58,388
include hiking, tennis, and running.

307
00:23:58,764 --> 00:24:02,351
But the outfits
for these hobbies look too sporty.

308
00:24:02,434 --> 00:24:03,435
So?

309
00:24:03,936 --> 00:24:04,937
What's your point?

310
00:24:06,647 --> 00:24:08,148
- Sorry?
- The key point.

311
00:24:09,191 --> 00:24:10,192
The key point...

312
00:24:16,156 --> 00:24:19,076
The visual concept
for the next season

313
00:24:19,826 --> 00:24:21,078
is camping.

314
00:24:22,871 --> 00:24:23,997
Okay, camping.

315
00:24:24,790 --> 00:24:25,958
Sounds great.

316
00:24:26,041 --> 00:24:27,167
From now on

317
00:24:28,043 --> 00:24:30,671
please do not spend
over a minute on your presentation.

318
00:24:31,129 --> 00:24:32,923
I'm not looking for

319
00:24:33,006 --> 00:24:36,176
an elaborate speech,
but the actual result of your work.

320
00:24:38,095 --> 00:24:39,262
Yes, sir.

321
00:24:39,721 --> 00:24:40,973
Are we done here?

322
00:24:41,473 --> 00:24:43,517
- Yes.
- This week

323
00:24:43,934 --> 00:24:45,894
I expect everyone to go all-in
on the Appello fashion show.

324
00:24:46,395 --> 00:24:48,021
It would be nice to film
what the venue is like

325
00:24:48,105 --> 00:24:49,940
and upload it to our official
social media accounts.

326
00:24:50,023 --> 00:24:51,024
Any volunteers?

327
00:24:55,779 --> 00:24:59,449
Lastly, Mr. Kang likes
those who take the initiative.

328
00:24:59,533 --> 00:25:01,743
Someone who steps up
and tries to make things happen.

329
00:25:02,202 --> 00:25:03,286
I will

330
00:25:03,787 --> 00:25:04,788
do it.

331
00:25:07,040 --> 00:25:09,835
Other people have a lot of work to do

332
00:25:09,918 --> 00:25:11,336
so I'll do it.

333
00:25:11,837 --> 00:25:13,505
Yes, she has been assisting

334
00:25:13,588 --> 00:25:15,841
with the management
of our social media account

335
00:25:15,924 --> 00:25:17,134
so it'll help.

336
00:25:21,680 --> 00:25:22,681
All right, then.

337
00:25:24,933 --> 00:25:26,351
We'll go and see the rehearsal today

338
00:25:26,810 --> 00:25:28,770
so be at my office by two o'clock.

339
00:25:28,854 --> 00:25:29,855
Yes, sir.

340
00:25:30,731 --> 00:25:32,315
Hey, Da-reum.

341
00:25:32,733 --> 00:25:35,610
It's your first time on site.
Are you sure you'll be fine?

342
00:25:37,320 --> 00:25:38,530
Mr. Kang.

343
00:25:39,865 --> 00:25:42,117
I think I should probably go.

344
00:25:42,200 --> 00:25:43,410
Let's give the volunteer a try.

345
00:25:46,288 --> 00:25:47,289
That's all, then.

346
00:25:47,372 --> 00:25:48,457
- Yes.
- Yes.

347
00:25:50,959 --> 00:25:51,960
Good luck.

348
00:26:17,235 --> 00:26:18,278
Mr. Kang...

349
00:26:35,670 --> 00:26:37,130
Everything is so neatly organized

350
00:26:38,090 --> 00:26:39,800
as expected from the office's owner.

351
00:26:41,927 --> 00:26:43,762
I can't believe I spent a night here.

352
00:26:55,732 --> 00:26:58,360
I want to be an outstanding employee
to join this trip.

353
00:27:06,493 --> 00:27:08,120
Wait, what?

354
00:27:09,412 --> 00:27:11,331
Why is he

355
00:27:11,957 --> 00:27:13,291
looking at him like that?

356
00:27:36,481 --> 00:27:37,732
What can I do

357
00:27:38,233 --> 00:27:40,318
to show you how I feel?

358
00:27:41,153 --> 00:27:43,238
I love you, Chan.

359
00:27:43,572 --> 00:27:46,867
- I love you, Chan.
- "I love you, Chan"?

360
00:28:11,016 --> 00:28:12,267
What can I do

361
00:28:13,185 --> 00:28:15,145
to show you how I feel?

362
00:28:17,272 --> 00:28:18,273
I love you...

363
00:28:20,567 --> 00:28:21,735
Chan.

364
00:28:29,784 --> 00:28:31,161
That blind item

365
00:28:32,454 --> 00:28:33,747
must be true.

366
00:28:36,416 --> 00:28:38,168
What do I do? What now?

367
00:28:50,222 --> 00:28:51,556
NO IMPORTANT DOCUMENT ON THE DESK

368
00:28:51,890 --> 00:28:53,683
- Did you wait long?
- Sorry?

369
00:28:54,351 --> 00:28:55,518
No, I just got here.

370
00:28:55,602 --> 00:28:59,689
I left the weekly meeting report
on your desk, sir.

371
00:29:11,534 --> 00:29:12,702
NO LEAKAGE OF CONFIDENTIAL INFO

372
00:29:19,125 --> 00:29:20,293
- Let's go.
- Sorry?

373
00:29:20,377 --> 00:29:22,295
Right. Yes.

374
00:29:22,879 --> 00:29:23,880
Let's go.

375
00:29:38,436 --> 00:29:39,437
- These days,
- Yes?

376
00:29:42,649 --> 00:29:44,359
is the job market tough?

377
00:29:46,736 --> 00:29:50,031
Yes, that's the case.

378
00:29:51,283 --> 00:29:54,035
Someone with your credentials
could've gone to major corporations.

379
00:29:54,119 --> 00:29:55,120
Gosh, hardly.

380
00:29:56,079 --> 00:29:57,163
By any chance

381
00:29:58,248 --> 00:30:00,333
any special reason
why you came to Appello?

382
00:30:03,753 --> 00:30:06,965
Actually, I wanted
to learn more about myself.

383
00:30:07,424 --> 00:30:09,009
Instead of just getting
more qualifications

384
00:30:09,092 --> 00:30:12,012
I wanted to find out
what I truly love.

385
00:30:12,262 --> 00:30:15,473
That was why I chose
to come to a place I was drawn to.

386
00:30:16,808 --> 00:30:17,851
Also

387
00:30:18,810 --> 00:30:22,147
there was someone
I really wanted to meet.

388
00:30:24,607 --> 00:30:25,775
Who is it?

389
00:30:27,444 --> 00:30:28,445
What?

390
00:30:30,572 --> 00:30:31,781
Did I just say it out loud?

391
00:30:31,865 --> 00:30:33,283
That was why I heard it.

392
00:30:38,455 --> 00:30:40,123
Well, what I meant

393
00:30:40,999 --> 00:30:44,377
was that I wanted to meet many people
in different industries on the job.

394
00:30:44,461 --> 00:30:45,837
Something like that.

395
00:30:50,091 --> 00:30:53,303
Mr. Kang, may I ask something too?

396
00:30:54,637 --> 00:30:55,638
Sure.

397
00:30:55,972 --> 00:30:58,808
Why did you come to Appello?

398
00:31:03,438 --> 00:31:06,274
At first,
it was because of one person.

399
00:31:07,025 --> 00:31:09,944
Could that be Chan?

400
00:31:10,028 --> 00:31:12,906
But now, Appello is my everything.

401
00:31:45,855 --> 00:31:47,690
- What's this? A prize draw?
- It's a prize draw.

402
00:31:47,774 --> 00:31:48,775
Thank you.

403
00:31:53,405 --> 00:31:54,531
My gosh. So that's how it looks.

404
00:31:56,324 --> 00:31:57,409
That's cool.

405
00:32:06,376 --> 00:32:07,877
That is so awesome.

406
00:32:09,421 --> 00:32:11,297
Is she putting on a show,
trying to look innocent?

407
00:32:12,841 --> 00:32:14,592
Goodness, Mr. Kang!

408
00:32:15,301 --> 00:32:18,346
I can't believe
you came all the way here yourself.

409
00:32:19,013 --> 00:32:20,807
- Hello.
- Of course, I should come.

410
00:32:21,057 --> 00:32:22,183
How's it coming along?

411
00:32:22,267 --> 00:32:23,435
Yes, of course.

412
00:32:24,018 --> 00:32:26,229
A new brand like ours
could never even dream

413
00:32:26,312 --> 00:32:27,439
of having a fashion show.

414
00:32:27,522 --> 00:32:29,983
Thank you very much
for giving us this great opportunity.

415
00:32:30,191 --> 00:32:32,819
Don't mention it.
Your brand already had the appeal.

416
00:32:32,902 --> 00:32:33,945
The opportunity simply found you.

417
00:32:35,447 --> 00:32:37,699
Anyway, I've never seen those before.

418
00:32:39,075 --> 00:32:42,036
This kind of event is a rare chance.

419
00:32:43,288 --> 00:32:46,958
So we even took out a loan
to make lots of new products.

420
00:32:47,876 --> 00:32:49,544
Although we wouldn't survive

421
00:32:49,627 --> 00:32:51,713
until the next season
if they end up as inventory.

422
00:32:52,297 --> 00:32:54,257
Oh, I almost jinxed it. Never mind.

423
00:32:54,340 --> 00:32:55,633
I won't let that happen.

424
00:32:55,717 --> 00:32:57,969
I'll make sure

425
00:32:58,052 --> 00:33:01,598
people see our products
and immediately go, "It's Go.Co."

426
00:33:01,681 --> 00:33:03,224
I will make it happen.

427
00:33:03,308 --> 00:33:04,517
I can do it!

428
00:33:05,059 --> 00:33:06,895
- Yes, please keep up the good work.
- Thanks.

429
00:33:06,978 --> 00:33:07,979
See you at the show.

430
00:33:08,062 --> 00:33:10,273
All right. Keep it up, Mr. Kang!

431
00:33:10,607 --> 00:33:11,816
- Let's go!
- Go for it!

432
00:33:18,281 --> 00:33:19,282
What are you smiling about?

433
00:33:21,951 --> 00:33:24,496
I had a thought that fashion brands

434
00:33:24,579 --> 00:33:27,081
and K-pop idol groups are similar.

435
00:33:27,999 --> 00:33:29,542
- K-pop idol?
- Yes.

436
00:33:30,543 --> 00:33:32,629
They show their presence on the stage

437
00:33:32,712 --> 00:33:35,340
bring thrills to people
with their visuals

438
00:33:35,423 --> 00:33:38,092
and above all, they're loved
by their fans for a very long time.

439
00:33:42,764 --> 00:33:45,225
Everyone must've put in
so much hard work

440
00:33:45,308 --> 00:33:47,519
just to get their chance
on that stage.

441
00:33:49,729 --> 00:33:51,898
I really hope this fashion show

442
00:33:52,398 --> 00:33:53,816
becomes a huge hit.

443
00:33:54,943 --> 00:33:57,195
I'll put in everything I have too.

444
00:34:14,420 --> 00:34:16,714
Now, let us begin!

445
00:34:17,173 --> 00:34:19,342
The first model, walk up to the spot.

446
00:34:19,425 --> 00:34:21,761
Maintain a three-second interval.
Now, go!

447
00:34:39,112 --> 00:34:40,655
Cool.

448
00:34:51,249 --> 00:34:52,500
- What happened?
- Cut.

449
00:34:52,584 --> 00:34:53,710
Are you okay?

450
00:34:53,793 --> 00:34:56,713
- Hey, go check on the model.
- Yes, sir.

451
00:34:57,505 --> 00:34:59,591
Reduce the amount of dry ice.

452
00:35:00,633 --> 00:35:03,845
- Was it because of dry ice?
- Yes, it looks like it.

453
00:35:03,928 --> 00:35:06,055
If too much dry ice is used,
it creates vapors.

454
00:35:10,476 --> 00:35:13,938
That's why he almost fell
on stage before.

455
00:35:14,022 --> 00:35:15,565
Let's wipe the stage.

456
00:35:15,648 --> 00:35:17,275
Can I have someone test the stage
before we begin?

457
00:35:17,358 --> 00:35:19,110
Anyone wearing dress shoes
among the staff?

458
00:35:25,742 --> 00:35:26,743
Can I do it?

459
00:35:26,826 --> 00:35:29,245
These heels are pretty low.
I think these will be okay.

460
00:35:29,871 --> 00:35:32,957
- Can I ask you to do it then?
- Of course.

461
00:35:33,041 --> 00:35:34,709
Why would you?

462
00:35:34,792 --> 00:35:36,544
If models get hurt, that will cause
problems for the show.

463
00:35:36,628 --> 00:35:38,421
I'll go walk slowly.

464
00:35:38,504 --> 00:35:41,382
- Do I start behind the stage?
- Yes. Thank you.

465
00:36:00,360 --> 00:36:01,569
Oh, no.

466
00:36:08,826 --> 00:36:09,827
Ms. Nam!

467
00:36:35,895 --> 00:36:37,480
- Are you okay?
- Yes.

468
00:36:38,189 --> 00:36:39,899
Oh, yes. I'm okay.

469
00:36:40,733 --> 00:36:43,653
You should've just walked.
Why did you make a turn?

470
00:36:43,736 --> 00:36:45,697
You almost hurt your head
from your carelessness.

471
00:36:47,907 --> 00:36:49,826
I know. Why did I do that?

472
00:36:52,578 --> 00:36:54,706
It's a bit watery over here.

473
00:36:54,789 --> 00:36:57,375
Someone should wipe over here.

474
00:36:57,458 --> 00:36:59,877
- Okay. Hey, go wipe it.
- Yes.

475
00:37:07,385 --> 00:37:10,179
We have Lee Chan playing the role

476
00:37:10,263 --> 00:37:12,765
of Seong-jun who appears
to be perfect in every way

477
00:37:12,849 --> 00:37:14,726
but actually clumsy and vulnerable
when it comes to love

478
00:37:14,809 --> 00:37:19,397
and Yoon Cho-yi who plays the role
of Yi-seo who matures by experiencing

479
00:37:19,480 --> 00:37:21,315
the sweetest moment
as well as the most bitter breakup.

480
00:37:21,399 --> 00:37:24,110
The two lead roles of Bitter Sweet.
Can you please make a heart?

481
00:37:26,529 --> 00:37:27,947
Can you look to the left?

482
00:37:28,489 --> 00:37:29,532
Now, to the center.

483
00:37:29,991 --> 00:37:31,075
To the right, please.

484
00:37:31,826 --> 00:37:33,286
Very nice.

485
00:37:34,579 --> 00:37:36,247
It's time for questions.

486
00:37:36,330 --> 00:37:38,708
If you have any questions,
please raise your hands

487
00:37:38,791 --> 00:37:40,084
and we'll pass you the mic.

488
00:37:40,710 --> 00:37:42,378
- Yes?
- Your unique chemistry was

489
00:37:42,462 --> 00:37:44,672
already evident in the preview.

490
00:37:44,756 --> 00:37:46,424
I wonder if you grew any feelings
for each other

491
00:37:46,507 --> 00:37:49,135
while working on this film.

492
00:37:49,427 --> 00:37:53,598
Well, to be honest, who wouldn't be
fluttered to see Lee Chan?

493
00:37:54,223 --> 00:37:57,018
I've been a fan of his
for a long time

494
00:37:57,101 --> 00:37:59,896
so that helped me focus
on portraying my emotions.

495
00:38:02,482 --> 00:38:04,108
Well, Ms. Cho-yi is very lovely.

496
00:38:04,567 --> 00:38:06,694
I think this drama did a good job

497
00:38:06,778 --> 00:38:08,738
of showcasing her charms.

498
00:38:08,821 --> 00:38:12,074
If I meet someone like her
in real life

499
00:38:13,910 --> 00:38:15,745
I can't help but fall in love.

500
00:38:19,832 --> 00:38:22,585
LEE CHAN AND YOON CHO-YI
GETTING FLUTTERED WHILE FILMING?

501
00:38:24,170 --> 00:38:25,963
Good job today.

502
00:38:26,047 --> 00:38:27,465
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

503
00:38:27,548 --> 00:38:28,591
See you later.

504
00:38:28,674 --> 00:38:30,092
- Bye.
- Bye.

505
00:38:33,805 --> 00:38:35,515
Good work, Mr. Lee.

506
00:38:36,098 --> 00:38:37,350
Yes, good work.

507
00:38:43,689 --> 00:38:44,941
Give me a second.

508
00:38:51,906 --> 00:38:54,534
Did you receive the gift I sent you?

509
00:38:55,159 --> 00:38:56,619
I gave it to my friend.

510
00:38:57,036 --> 00:38:58,037
What?

511
00:39:00,122 --> 00:39:02,583
You've been ignoring my calls.
How long will you keep doing this?

512
00:39:03,000 --> 00:39:04,043
Cho-yi.

513
00:39:05,795 --> 00:39:06,838
We broke up.

514
00:39:07,672 --> 00:39:09,549
- It's time for you to accept it.
- No.

515
00:39:10,633 --> 00:39:14,053
I can't break up with you.
No, I'm not breaking up with you.

516
00:39:14,929 --> 00:39:16,722
I really loved you.

517
00:39:16,806 --> 00:39:18,307
Are you saying you didn't love me?

518
00:39:19,225 --> 00:39:20,351
Not even for a moment?

519
00:39:20,685 --> 00:39:22,186
I did have feelings for you.

520
00:39:22,770 --> 00:39:25,439
But it wasn't love.

521
00:39:25,523 --> 00:39:26,691
But why?

522
00:39:27,608 --> 00:39:29,235
What do I lack?

523
00:39:31,696 --> 00:39:33,531
It's not that you lacked anything.

524
00:39:33,823 --> 00:39:35,366
We just weren't right for each other.

525
00:39:35,867 --> 00:39:36,868
Cho-yi.

526
00:39:38,244 --> 00:39:41,539
You're perfect
just the way you are, okay?

527
00:39:46,377 --> 00:39:49,714
Do you know how much I struggled
and endured to put up with you?

528
00:39:50,464 --> 00:39:51,799
Are you saying
I wasn't right for you?

529
00:39:51,883 --> 00:39:54,427
Do you think all that struggling
and enduring means love?

530
00:39:56,137 --> 00:39:58,556
Someone who lets you be yourself.

531
00:39:59,891 --> 00:40:01,100
Find someone like that.

532
00:40:03,811 --> 00:40:05,187
This is ridiculous.

533
00:40:05,271 --> 00:40:07,607
You pretend to be polite and sweet.

534
00:40:08,441 --> 00:40:10,776
But you're just pretending
to be the better person to leave me.

535
00:40:12,028 --> 00:40:13,029
...I

536
00:40:14,280 --> 00:40:15,740
I won't ever break up with you.

537
00:40:16,991 --> 00:40:18,284
So...

538
00:40:19,660 --> 00:40:20,953
you might as well endure it.

539
00:41:00,242 --> 00:41:03,079
Well, should I play some music?

540
00:41:03,788 --> 00:41:05,122
Oh, yes. I'd love that.

541
00:41:10,169 --> 00:41:11,337
What...

542
00:41:13,339 --> 00:41:15,383
Why is this...

543
00:41:19,845 --> 00:41:20,846
INCOMING CALL
LEE CHAN

544
00:41:24,475 --> 00:41:25,726
ANSWER

545
00:41:26,268 --> 00:41:27,853
- Hello?
- Where are you?

546
00:41:28,729 --> 00:41:30,064
It's really Chan.

547
00:41:30,147 --> 00:41:32,108
I'm almost at work. Where are you?

548
00:41:32,441 --> 00:41:34,527
Me? Not sure.

549
00:41:35,528 --> 00:41:37,989
What? We spent all night together.
But do you miss me already?

550
00:41:38,739 --> 00:41:40,032
"All night"?

551
00:41:44,286 --> 00:41:46,497
Hey, stop joking around, will you?

552
00:41:46,580 --> 00:41:49,750
What? We were good together
until this morning.

553
00:41:50,126 --> 00:41:51,544
Until this morning?

554
00:41:51,627 --> 00:41:53,087
By the way,
what am I supposed to pick up?

555
00:41:53,170 --> 00:41:54,714
Whatever. I'll throw it out.

556
00:41:54,797 --> 00:41:56,007
You're better off without seeing it.

557
00:42:00,469 --> 00:42:04,056
What can I do to show you how I feel?

558
00:42:04,807 --> 00:42:06,767
I love you, Chan.

559
00:42:13,482 --> 00:42:16,819
Is he throwing out that card?

560
00:42:19,655 --> 00:42:21,240
The power is off.

561
00:42:59,403 --> 00:43:00,696
I can't believe

562
00:43:01,739 --> 00:43:03,657
Mr. Kang was in love with Chan.

563
00:43:08,162 --> 00:43:10,664
How did I end up
finding out this secret?

564
00:43:13,959 --> 00:43:14,960
You're still here?

565
00:43:46,075 --> 00:43:47,535
Director Lee.

566
00:43:47,618 --> 00:43:48,702
Have you been well?

567
00:43:51,539 --> 00:43:52,540
Yes.

568
00:43:55,835 --> 00:43:57,128
Oh, hello.

569
00:44:01,841 --> 00:44:04,844
Who was your favorite in D.N.X?

570
00:44:05,136 --> 00:44:06,387
Well...

571
00:44:07,304 --> 00:44:08,305
Pardon?

572
00:44:10,015 --> 00:44:11,350
How did you know that?

573
00:44:11,433 --> 00:44:13,477
You're listening to our song
from ten years ago.

574
00:44:21,152 --> 00:44:22,486
By any chance...

575
00:44:26,031 --> 00:44:27,158
was it me?

576
00:44:37,251 --> 00:44:38,252
Right?

577
00:44:40,754 --> 00:44:41,755
It was.

578
00:44:42,923 --> 00:44:44,133
I'm doomed.

579
00:44:44,216 --> 00:44:45,426
Gosh...

580
00:44:49,263 --> 00:44:52,349
How did you get that right
on your first try?

581
00:44:52,641 --> 00:44:54,935
Just my gut feeling.

582
00:44:58,189 --> 00:45:00,816
Oh, my gosh. That's crazy.

583
00:45:02,902 --> 00:45:05,112
You must've been a fan
since you were a kid.

584
00:45:06,572 --> 00:45:08,365
You can call me Chan
when it's just the two of us.

585
00:45:08,449 --> 00:45:10,159
Oh, no. Still...

586
00:45:10,534 --> 00:45:11,911
I will

587
00:45:13,370 --> 00:45:15,289
call you Da-reum.
Is that okay with you?

588
00:45:19,919 --> 00:45:20,920
Yes.

589
00:45:22,087 --> 00:45:23,255
Chan.

590
00:45:26,967 --> 00:45:30,012
It's been over ten years
since D.N.X disbanded.

591
00:45:30,095 --> 00:45:32,264
I didn't know there was still someone
who listened to our music.

592
00:45:33,015 --> 00:45:34,016
Thank you.

593
00:45:36,143 --> 00:45:39,230
I've listened to it for so long

594
00:45:39,313 --> 00:45:41,106
that it's become part of my routine.

595
00:45:41,482 --> 00:45:43,108
When I'm walking or working

596
00:45:44,443 --> 00:45:46,987
I find myself listening to it
without even realizing it.

597
00:45:48,197 --> 00:45:50,032
NAM DA-REUM

598
00:45:54,828 --> 00:45:56,622
- Give me your phone.
- What?

599
00:46:05,172 --> 00:46:07,132
I left it in the office.

600
00:46:45,754 --> 00:46:46,797
There.

601
00:46:53,846 --> 00:46:54,847
Call me.

602
00:46:58,600 --> 00:46:59,601
I will.

603
00:47:04,773 --> 00:47:05,858
You promise?

604
00:47:10,696 --> 00:47:12,281
No way.

605
00:47:13,073 --> 00:47:14,074
Awesome.

606
00:47:14,825 --> 00:47:17,036
Is this really Chan's number?

607
00:47:18,120 --> 00:47:19,121
Yes.

608
00:47:19,747 --> 00:47:22,249
Hey. Namda.

609
00:47:24,043 --> 00:47:25,419
She's completely out of it.

610
00:47:25,711 --> 00:47:27,254
A celeb giving you his number?

611
00:47:27,463 --> 00:47:28,756
What's that supposed to mean?

612
00:47:29,048 --> 00:47:31,258
He told you to call him.
Call him and find out.

613
00:47:33,093 --> 00:47:36,055
I doubt he really meant it.

614
00:47:36,138 --> 00:47:38,390
It's just that I work for his company

615
00:47:39,016 --> 00:47:40,517
and I'm an old fan, so...

616
00:47:40,601 --> 00:47:41,602
So?

617
00:47:44,104 --> 00:47:45,314
Oh, I don't know.

618
00:47:45,397 --> 00:47:48,650
Maybe he gave it to you
because he had a crush on you.

619
00:47:48,734 --> 00:47:50,527
- What?
- She's right.

620
00:47:50,861 --> 00:47:52,738
He could've saved your number
on his phone.

621
00:47:52,821 --> 00:47:54,531
Why did he have to do that?

622
00:47:54,615 --> 00:47:55,949
Why did he write it on your hand?

623
00:47:56,033 --> 00:47:57,201
He was totally flirting.

624
00:47:57,284 --> 00:48:00,788
Hey. He wasn't.
That's totally not true.

625
00:48:01,205 --> 00:48:02,206
First things first.

626
00:48:03,707 --> 00:48:04,708
Let's save it.

627
00:48:06,543 --> 00:48:07,753
Don't do anything other than saving.

628
00:48:15,844 --> 00:48:18,055
What the? Are you really calling him?

629
00:48:18,138 --> 00:48:19,473
Hey. No. Stop it.

630
00:48:19,556 --> 00:48:22,142
Are you nuts? Get back here.
Give it to me.

631
00:48:22,226 --> 00:48:23,394
Hey.

632
00:48:25,896 --> 00:48:28,357
What do I do? What am I going to say?

633
00:48:32,152 --> 00:48:33,445
Hello?

634
00:48:37,616 --> 00:48:39,243
Chan?

635
00:48:39,326 --> 00:48:42,121
It's me, Da-reum.

636
00:48:44,248 --> 00:48:45,457
Hello?

637
00:48:53,757 --> 00:48:56,135
Isn't this Director Lee's number?

638
00:48:56,552 --> 00:48:57,761
Director Lee?

639
00:48:58,804 --> 00:49:00,514
Yes, this is his number.

640
00:49:04,268 --> 00:49:08,981
I work for Director Lee's company.

641
00:49:09,064 --> 00:49:11,817
Oh, my Chan?

642
00:49:12,401 --> 00:49:13,735
He's in the shower.

643
00:49:19,950 --> 00:49:21,160
Sorry about that.

644
00:49:25,539 --> 00:49:28,250
Saying you work for him
after calling him Chan?

645
00:49:29,001 --> 00:49:30,002
That's beyond ridiculous.

646
00:49:30,085 --> 00:49:31,628
DELETE THIS CONTACT?

647
00:49:36,216 --> 00:49:37,468
BITTER SWEET

648
00:49:37,551 --> 00:49:38,719
What's the next scene?

649
00:49:38,802 --> 00:49:40,637
Prepare it thoroughly...

650
00:49:46,894 --> 00:49:48,395
What are you doing in my green room?

651
00:49:48,479 --> 00:49:49,605
The next scene.

652
00:49:50,272 --> 00:49:51,607
Will you help me rehearse?

653
00:49:53,567 --> 00:49:54,776
We still need to do our job.

654
00:49:54,860 --> 00:49:56,195
- Do you want to grab coffee?
- Let's get coffee.

655
00:50:04,786 --> 00:50:05,787
Namda.

656
00:50:09,041 --> 00:50:11,543
I told you not to call him. See?

657
00:50:11,627 --> 00:50:14,880
Why did he lead you on
when he has a girlfriend?

658
00:50:14,963 --> 00:50:16,465
I told you it wasn't like that.

659
00:50:16,757 --> 00:50:18,800
You're the same.

660
00:50:20,219 --> 00:50:22,471
Look what you've done.

661
00:50:22,971 --> 00:50:24,515
I'm doomed.

662
00:50:25,057 --> 00:50:27,226
Oh, I'm doomed.

663
00:50:27,518 --> 00:50:30,312
- It's your fault.
- Why did you do that?

664
00:50:30,395 --> 00:50:33,941
- You called him.
- Because you told me to.

665
00:50:35,317 --> 00:50:36,401
But you know what

666
00:50:37,861 --> 00:50:38,904
this is for the better.

667
00:50:39,613 --> 00:50:42,783
If Chan answered,
it would've been really awkward.

668
00:50:43,158 --> 00:50:44,243
Namda.

669
00:50:45,702 --> 00:50:46,703
You're not disappointed?

670
00:50:48,247 --> 00:50:51,208
Chan is human after all.
Of course, he can have a girlfriend.

671
00:50:51,458 --> 00:50:54,545
I actually want him to meet someone

672
00:50:55,128 --> 00:50:56,296
and be happy.

673
00:51:01,134 --> 00:51:04,596
Hey. A true fan is different.

674
00:51:04,972 --> 00:51:06,682
I approve.

675
00:51:09,017 --> 00:51:10,018
What time is it?

676
00:51:11,019 --> 00:51:12,271
Hey. It's time for Chan's drama.

677
00:51:12,354 --> 00:51:13,814
It's the first episode.
Make sure you stay for it.

678
00:51:32,374 --> 00:51:33,417
Hey.

679
00:51:35,502 --> 00:51:37,212
What's that look on your face?

680
00:51:37,921 --> 00:51:40,090
Are you out of your mind? Hey.

681
00:51:40,465 --> 00:51:42,593
Who are you to be disappointed?

682
00:51:42,676 --> 00:51:44,845
You've been a fan for 12 years.

683
00:51:44,928 --> 00:51:46,263
Get a grip.

684
00:51:56,898 --> 00:51:59,443
What if my call interrupted him?

685
00:52:00,360 --> 00:52:02,529
I hope
he doesn't think I'm a crazy fan.

686
00:52:04,531 --> 00:52:06,491
Oh, forget it.
I don't want to think about it.

687
00:52:21,340 --> 00:52:22,341
Hold on.

688
00:52:22,758 --> 00:52:24,885
I love you, Chan.

689
00:52:27,638 --> 00:52:29,389
If Chan has a girlfriend...

690
00:52:31,767 --> 00:52:33,018
what about Mr. Kang?

691
00:52:36,355 --> 00:52:38,523
Is it one-sided?

692
00:52:42,527 --> 00:52:44,946
That's pitiful.

693
00:52:47,407 --> 00:52:48,533
Oh, gosh.

694
00:53:04,800 --> 00:53:06,843
SUNGJU

695
00:53:26,488 --> 00:53:28,031
Here's your Americano.

696
00:53:30,033 --> 00:53:31,243
Thank you.

697
00:53:53,473 --> 00:53:56,143
How long has he been bottling
his feelings alone?

698
00:53:56,935 --> 00:53:58,103
Did he want to stay by his side

699
00:53:58,603 --> 00:54:00,230
even as a friend?

700
00:54:20,208 --> 00:54:22,586
Mr. Kang, have this

701
00:54:23,253 --> 00:54:24,421
and cheer up.

702
00:54:25,005 --> 00:54:26,006
Good luck.

703
00:54:39,186 --> 00:54:40,270
Mr. Kang.

704
00:54:41,521 --> 00:54:43,857
Mr. Kang. Were you looking for me?

705
00:54:45,400 --> 00:54:46,610
It's been up there for too long.

706
00:54:46,943 --> 00:54:48,403
I've seen it for too long,
it's not so impressive anymore.

707
00:54:49,821 --> 00:54:52,240
Okay, I'll replace it
as soon as possible.

708
00:54:55,786 --> 00:54:58,538
I thought you didn't drink coffee.
What's gotten into you?

709
00:54:59,873 --> 00:55:02,167
Well, it's not so bad.

710
00:55:05,837 --> 00:55:07,172
Good. One, two.

711
00:55:07,589 --> 00:55:10,008
Good. Look at the window. One, two.

712
00:55:10,091 --> 00:55:11,134
Nice.

713
00:55:11,218 --> 00:55:12,344
Fix his hair, please.

714
00:55:13,470 --> 00:55:15,764
Nice. One, two. Smile a bit.

715
00:55:15,847 --> 00:55:17,557
One, two. Excellent.

716
00:55:17,641 --> 00:55:19,100
One more. One, two.

717
00:55:19,476 --> 00:55:20,519
Good job.

718
00:55:21,978 --> 00:55:25,232
- I just love the photos today.
- The colors looked perfect.

719
00:55:26,566 --> 00:55:28,443
- Let me get ready for the next set.
- Okay.

720
00:55:29,486 --> 00:55:31,530
- Hey. Can I have my phone?
- Yes.

721
00:55:33,073 --> 00:55:34,741
- Did I get any calls?
- No.

722
00:55:35,659 --> 00:55:37,035
Are you expecting one?

723
00:55:38,245 --> 00:55:39,329
No.

724
00:55:39,412 --> 00:55:40,914
UNREAD

725
00:55:40,997 --> 00:55:42,582
I just wanted to treat her to a meal.

726
00:55:45,001 --> 00:55:47,003
- Who?
- Just...

727
00:55:48,672 --> 00:55:51,049
Someone I'm grateful to.

728
00:55:53,343 --> 00:55:57,430
Mr. Kang, please confirm the location
for the fashion show.

729
00:55:57,514 --> 00:55:58,515
Sure.

730
00:56:04,354 --> 00:56:06,189
Mr. Kang, do you drink coffee now?

731
00:56:08,984 --> 00:56:11,027
Yes, it happened somehow.

732
00:56:11,862 --> 00:56:13,780
- You may proceed.
- Thank you.

733
00:56:15,073 --> 00:56:16,157
Wait...

734
00:56:16,950 --> 00:56:17,993
Yes, sir.

735
00:56:18,994 --> 00:56:21,121
How is Nam Da-reum doing?

736
00:56:22,205 --> 00:56:23,707
In terms of work and all.

737
00:56:26,042 --> 00:56:27,252
I think

738
00:56:27,669 --> 00:56:29,170
she's very diligent.

739
00:56:29,254 --> 00:56:31,631
She always takes initiative
and does her best in everything.

740
00:56:32,382 --> 00:56:33,925
She's very cheerful.

741
00:56:37,053 --> 00:56:38,221
She actually asked me

742
00:56:38,305 --> 00:56:40,724
about how to become
the outstanding employee.

743
00:56:41,266 --> 00:56:42,434
The outstanding employee?

744
00:56:43,018 --> 00:56:44,019
Yes.

745
00:56:55,572 --> 00:56:57,532
- Are the materials ready?
- Yes.

746
00:56:57,866 --> 00:56:59,826
- Won-tae, let's go.
- Okay.

747
00:57:05,081 --> 00:57:07,792
Da-reum, have you sorted out
the messenger promotion message

748
00:57:07,876 --> 00:57:11,338
- on the Appello fashion show?
- Oh, yes.

749
00:57:11,421 --> 00:57:14,382
I prepared two reminder versions
for the day of the show.

750
00:57:14,466 --> 00:57:15,550
Give me one second.

751
00:57:26,728 --> 00:57:27,938
MESSENGER

752
00:57:29,189 --> 00:57:30,231
NO RESULTS FOUND

753
00:57:32,817 --> 00:57:34,653
- What's taking so long?
- I...

754
00:57:37,072 --> 00:57:38,531
The files are gone.

755
00:57:40,867 --> 00:57:41,993
Gone?

756
00:57:42,327 --> 00:57:43,411
Yes.

757
00:57:46,247 --> 00:57:47,332
I'll make them quickly.

758
00:57:47,415 --> 00:57:49,042
I've already done it once.
It won't take long.

759
00:57:49,417 --> 00:57:52,128
Did you actually do it?

760
00:57:59,094 --> 00:58:02,180
We're updating it tomorrow.
Make sure to send it to me by today.

761
00:58:04,182 --> 00:58:05,433
I'm sorry.

762
00:58:09,980 --> 00:58:13,233
Did someone touch my computer?

763
00:58:13,984 --> 00:58:16,194
No, I doubt it.

764
00:58:17,612 --> 00:58:18,989
I probably lost it.

765
00:58:31,793 --> 00:58:33,211
APPELLO FASHION SHOW
MESSENGER MESSAGE PROPOSAL

766
00:58:37,173 --> 00:58:39,134
I won't have a chance
of becoming an outstanding employee

767
00:58:39,926 --> 00:58:41,678
let alone an ordinary employee.

768
00:58:50,687 --> 00:58:53,064
How can he work overtime every day?

769
00:58:55,567 --> 00:58:57,569
Seriously, that's amazing.

770
00:59:10,582 --> 00:59:11,708
That's strange.

771
00:59:12,292 --> 00:59:15,503
I swear it was on the wallpaper.

772
00:59:20,967 --> 00:59:22,969
What? I'm just borrowing this.

773
00:59:23,928 --> 00:59:24,971
Okay.

774
00:59:38,359 --> 00:59:39,360
No.

775
00:59:39,903 --> 00:59:40,987
Oh, no.

776
00:59:42,906 --> 00:59:44,199
Don't overthink it.

777
00:59:51,498 --> 00:59:53,124
JANGSHINCHEON, GUDORIM

778
01:00:46,427 --> 01:00:49,264
INGUK STATION

779
01:00:50,974 --> 01:00:52,016
Mr. Kang.

780
01:00:52,725 --> 01:00:53,726
Don't you have an umbrella?

781
01:00:54,310 --> 01:00:56,146
What brings you here

782
01:00:56,229 --> 01:00:58,565
- I live around here.
- Really? Me too.

783
01:00:59,065 --> 01:01:00,650
Let's go. I'll walk you home.

784
01:01:00,733 --> 01:01:01,943
Oh, no. It's okay.

785
01:01:02,402 --> 01:01:04,279
- Then will you go on your own?
- What?

786
01:01:05,196 --> 01:01:06,197
No.

787
01:01:16,374 --> 01:01:18,585
What happened to your car?
Why did you take the subway?

788
01:01:19,210 --> 01:01:20,378
It's in the body shop.

789
01:01:22,463 --> 01:01:23,882
Did you work overtime today?

790
01:01:24,883 --> 01:01:26,050
Yes, a little.

791
01:01:27,927 --> 01:01:30,388
If you're getting home now,
it wasn't just a little overtime.

792
01:01:32,182 --> 01:01:33,725
Is there too much work to do?

793
01:01:33,808 --> 01:01:35,226
Oh, no.

794
01:01:35,977 --> 01:01:38,062
It's just that I made a mistake.

795
01:01:40,607 --> 01:01:44,986
I bet you never make any mistakes
because you're thorough.

796
01:01:45,278 --> 01:01:46,654
You're right. I don't.

797
01:01:49,616 --> 01:01:52,327
But I used to make a lot of mistakes
when I was a newbie.

798
01:01:53,828 --> 01:01:56,080
You make mistakes
because you're doing the job.

799
01:01:57,582 --> 01:01:58,917
If you don't do anything

